## Deriving ADAE from AE + ADSL

ADAE (Adverse Events Analysis Dataset) is built by merging the SDTM **AE** domain with the subject-level **ADSL** (to bring in treatment exposure dates `TRTSDT`/`TRTEDT`, `TRTA`/`TRTP`, demography, and `SAFFL`), then layering analysis-period flags and imputed dates on top.

Below is a complete, commented **SAS** derivation (the canonical language for ADaM), followed by the rule for each variable and a compact **R `{admiral}`** alternative.

---

### Full SAS program

```sas
/* ---------------------------------------------------------------
   ADAE : Adverse Events Analysis Dataset
   Inputs : AE (SDTM), ADSL (subject-level)
   --------------------------------------------------------------- */

/* 0. Sort + merge AE with ADSL -------------------------------- */
proc sort data = ae;     by usubjid; run;
proc sort data = adsl;   by usubjid; run;

%let trtvar = trta trtp trtan trtpn trtsdt trtedt saffl age sex race;

data adae0;
    length astdtf aendtf $1 trtemfl aoccfl aoccpfl $1
           aduru $8;
    format astdt aendt yymmdd10.;

    merge ae(in = a) adsl(in = b keep = usubjid &trtvar);
    by usubjid;
    if a;                          /* keep AE records only            */

    /* ---- 2. ASTDT / AENDT : char(ISO) -> numeric + partial imputation ---- */
    /* Start date : impute missing day -> 01, missing month -> Jan 01      */
    if      length(aestdtc) = 10 then astdt = input(aestdtc, yymmdd10.);
    else if length(aestdtc) =  7 then do;            /* YYYY-MM  */
        astdt  = input(cats(aestdtc,'-01'), yymmdd10.);
        astdtf = 'D';
    end;
    else if length(aestdtc) =  4 then do;            /* YYYY     */
        astdt  = input(cats(aestdtc,'-01-01'), yymmdd10.);
        astdtf = 'M';            /* month is the most precise imputed part */
    end;

    /* End date : impute missing day -> last day of month, missing month -> Dec 31 */
    if      length(aeendtc) = 10 then aendt = input(aeendtc, yymmdd10.);
    else if length(aeendtc) =  7 then do;            /* YYYY-MM  */
        _nextmo = intnx('month', input(cats(aeendtc,'-01'), yymmdd10.), 1);
        aendt   = _nextmo - 1;                       /* last day of month */
        aendtf  = 'D';
    end;
    else if length(aeendtc) =  4 then do;            /* YYYY     */
        aendt  = input(cats(aeendtc,'-12-31'), yymmdd10.);
        aendtf = 'M';
    end;

    /* ---- 4. ADURN / ADURU : analysis duration in days ------------------- */
    if not missing(astdt) and not missing(aendt) then do;
        adurn = aendt - astdt + 1;
        aduru = 'DAYS';
    end;

    /* ---- 1. TRTEMFL : treatment-emergent (AE start >= first dose) ------- */
    if not missing(astdt) and not missing(trtsdt) then do;
        if astdt >= trtsdt then trtemfl = 'Y';
    end;
    else if missing(astdt) then trtemfl = 'Y';        /* conservative:
                                                         cannot prove it
                                                         pre-dated dosing  */
run;

/* ---- 3. AOCCFL : first AE overall (1 per subject, TE only) ------------- */
proc sort data = adae0; by usubjid astdt aeseq; run;
data adae1;
    set adae0;
    by usubjid;
    if first.usubjid and trtemfl = 'Y' then aoccfl = 'Y';
run;

/* ---- 3. AOCCPFL : first AE by Preferred Term (TE only) ----------------- */
proc sort data = adae1; by usubjid aedecod astdt aeseq; run;
data adae;
    set adae1;
    by usubjid aedecod;
    if first.aedecod and trtemfl = 'Y' then aoccpfl = 'Y';

    /* keep analysis view */
    keep studyid usubjid aeseq &trtvar aestdtc aeendtc
         astdt astdtf aendt aendtf trtemfl adurn aduru
         aoccfl aoccpfl aedecod aesoc aesev aeser aerel aeout aeterm;
run;
```

---

### Derivation rules

| # | Variable | Rule |
|---|----------|------|
| 1 | **TRTEMFL** | `= "Y"` when `ASTDT >= TRTSDT` (AE starts on/after first dose). If the start date is fully missing, a conservative rule flags it `"Y"` (cannot prove it pre-dated dosing); some sponsors leave it blank or compare imputed dates instead. |
| 2 | **ASTDT / AENDT** | Numeric SAS date from `AESTDTC`/`AEENDTC` (ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`). Partial dates are imputed: **start** → `01` for missing day, `Jan-01` for missing month; **end** → *last day of month* for missing day, `Dec-31` for missing month. Imputation parts recorded in `ASTDTF`/`AENDTF` (`"D"` = day imputed, `"M"` = month imputed — most precise element). |
| 3 | **AOCCFL** | `"Y"` on the chronologically **first** treatment-emergent AE per subject (`by USUBJID`, ordered by `ASTDT, AESEQ`). |
| 3 | **AOCCPFL** | `"Y"` on the **first occurrence of each Preferred Term** (`by USUBJID, AEDECOD`) among treatment-emergent AEs. |
| 4 | **ADURN / ADURU** | `ADURN = AENDT − ASTDT + 1` (inclusive, in days); `ADURU = "DAYS"`. Missing when either date is unavailable. |

Both occurrence flags are conventionally restricted to `TRTEMFL = "Y"` records because safety tables count treatment-emergent events.

